IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er1-interruption-of-earnings`

-- Tests of er1-interruption-of-earnings (Employment Insurance Regulations, regs 14 and 14.01). Piece er1.
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the Regulations (../../registers/source-bundle/SOR-96-332.txt), beside the assertion,
-- before the rule was run. The argument order is the order of the rule's GIVEN lines.
-- Calendar used below: Sunday 18 October 2026 begins a week, Saturday 24 October 2026 ends it, Sunday 25 October 2026 begins the next.

§ `The reasons (src:211, 223)`

#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the reason is a circumstance listed in subsection (2)` `er1 illness, injury or quarantine`
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the reason is a circumstance listed in subsection (2)` `er1 pregnancy`
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the reason is a circumstance listed in subsection (2)` `er1 the need to care for a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Act`
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the reason is a circumstance listed in subsection (2)` `er1 the need to provide care or support to a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) of the Act`
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the reason is a circumstance listed in subsection (2)` `er1 the need to provide care or support to a critically ill child`
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the reason is a circumstance listed in subsection (2)` `er1 the need to provide care or support to a critically ill adult`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14(2) the reason is a circumstance listed in subsection (2)` `er1 another reason`)
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the reason is a circumstance listed in regulation 14.01` `er1 self-employed illness, injury or quarantine`
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the reason is a circumstance listed in regulation 14.01` `er1 self-employed pregnancy`
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the reason is a circumstance listed in regulation 14.01` `er1 self-employed need to care for a child or children referred to in subsection 152.05(1) of the Act`
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the reason is a circumstance listed in regulation 14.01` `er1 self-employed need to provide care or support to a family member referred to in subsection 152.06(1) of the Act`
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the reason is a circumstance listed in regulation 14.01` `er1 self-employed need to provide care or support to a critically ill child`
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the reason is a circumstance listed in regulation 14.01` `er1 self-employed need to provide care or support to a critically ill adult`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14.01 the reason is a circumstance listed in regulation 14.01` `er1 self-employed another reason`)

§ `Regulation 14(1) - lay-off or separation (src:210)`

-- arguments: an insured person; this follows a period of employment with an employer; laid off; separated from that employment; the number of consecutive days with no work and no earnings
#ASSERT `reg 14(1) an interruption of earnings occurs on lay-off or separation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 7        -- laid off, seven days
#ASSERT `reg 14(1) an interruption of earnings occurs on lay-off or separation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 7        -- separated, seven days
#ASSERT `reg 14(1) an interruption of earnings occurs on lay-off or separation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 30
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14(1) an interruption of earnings occurs on lay-off or separation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 6)   -- "seven or more consecutive days": six is too few
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14(1) an interruption of earnings occurs on lay-off or separation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 10) -- neither laid off nor separated
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14(1) an interruption of earnings occurs on lay-off or separation` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 10) -- not an insured person
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14(1) an interruption of earnings occurs on lay-off or separation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 10) -- not "following a period of employment with an employer"

§ `Regulation 14(2) - a reduction in earnings of more than 40% (src:211)`

-- the reduction: arguments: normal weekly earnings; earnings for the week
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) a reduction in earnings that is more than 40% of the insured person's normal weekly earnings` 1000 599 -- reduction 401 is more than 400
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) a reduction in earnings that is more than 40% of the insured person's normal weekly earnings` 1000 0
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14(2) a reduction in earnings that is more than 40% of the insured person's normal weekly earnings` 1000 600)   -- reduction 400 is exactly 40%, not more
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14(2) a reduction in earnings that is more than 40% of the insured person's normal weekly earnings` 1000 1000)  -- no reduction
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14(2) a reduction in earnings that is more than 40% of the insured person's normal weekly earnings` 1000 1200)  -- earnings rose
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14(2) a reduction in earnings that is more than 40% of the insured person's normal weekly earnings` 0 0)        -- nothing to reduce
-- the day: arguments: an insured person; a day in the week of the reduction; normal weekly earnings; earnings for the week; ceases to work in that employment; the reason
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs because of a reduction in earnings` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 21) 1000 500 TRUE `er1 illness, injury or quarantine` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 18)   -- the beginning of the week
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs because of a reduction in earnings` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 18) 1000 500 TRUE `er1 pregnancy` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 18)                      -- a Sunday begins its own week
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs because of a reduction in earnings` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 24) 1000 500 TRUE `er1 the need to care for a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Act` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 18)   -- a Saturday ends it
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs because of a reduction in earnings` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 25) 1000 500 TRUE `er1 the need to provide care or support to a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) of the Act` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 25)
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs because of a reduction in earnings` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 21) 1000 500 TRUE `er1 the need to provide care or support to a critically ill child` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 18)
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs because of a reduction in earnings` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 21) 1000 500 TRUE `er1 the need to provide care or support to a critically ill adult` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 18)
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs because of a reduction in earnings` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 21) 1000 600 TRUE `er1 illness, injury or quarantine` EQUALS NOTHING          -- exactly 40%
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs because of a reduction in earnings` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 21) 1000 500 TRUE `er1 another reason` EQUALS NOTHING                    -- a reason not listed
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs because of a reduction in earnings` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 21) 1000 500 FALSE `er1 illness, injury or quarantine` EQUALS NOTHING         -- did not cease to work in that employment
#ASSERT `reg 14(2) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs because of a reduction in earnings` FALSE (YMD 2026 10 21) 1000 500 TRUE `er1 illness, injury or quarantine` EQUALS NOTHING        -- not an insured person

§ `Regulation 14(3), (4) and (6) - no interruption (src:212, 213, 221)`

#ASSERT `reg 14(3) a period of leave referred to in subsection 11(4) of the Act does not constitute an interruption of earnings` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14(3) a period of leave referred to in subsection 11(4) of the Act does not constitute an interruption of earnings` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 14(6) a period of leave referred to in subsection 11(3) of the Act does not constitute an interruption of earnings` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14(6) a period of leave referred to in subsection 11(3) of the Act does not constitute an interruption of earnings` FALSE)
-- (4) arguments: employed under a contract of employment; days in the period for which the usual remuneration is payable; the time in question falls during that period
#ASSERT `reg 14(4) no interruption of earnings occurs during a period greater than a week for which the usual remuneration is payable` TRUE 8 TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 14(4) no interruption of earnings occurs during a period greater than a week for which the usual remuneration is payable` TRUE 30 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14(4) no interruption of earnings occurs during a period greater than a week for which the usual remuneration is payable` TRUE 7 TRUE)    -- a period of a week is not "greater than a week"
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14(4) no interruption of earnings occurs during a period greater than a week for which the usual remuneration is payable` TRUE 14 FALSE)  -- the time is not during that period
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14(4) no interruption of earnings occurs during a period greater than a week for which the usual remuneration is payable` FALSE 14 TRUE)  -- no contract of employment

§ `Regulation 14(5) - commission earners (src:214-220)`

-- (a) arguments: real estate on a commission basis; holds a provincial licence; licence surrendered, suspended or revoked; ceases to work by reason of a circumstance in (2); the day it happens
#ASSERT `reg 14(5)(a) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs for a real estate salesperson on commission` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 10 21) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 21)
#ASSERT `reg 14(5)(a) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs for a real estate salesperson on commission` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 10 22) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 22)
#ASSERT `reg 14(5)(a) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs for a real estate salesperson on commission` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 10 21) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 14(5)(a) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs for a real estate salesperson on commission` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 10 21) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 14(5)(a) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs for a real estate salesperson on commission` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 10 21) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no provincial licence
-- (b) arguments: employed under a contract of employment; earnings mainly commissions; the contract is terminated; ceases to work by reason of a circumstance in (2); the day it happens
#ASSERT `reg 14(5)(b) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs for a person whose earnings are mainly commissions` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 10 21) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 21)
#ASSERT `reg 14(5)(b) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs for a person whose earnings are mainly commissions` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 10 23) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 23)
#ASSERT `reg 14(5)(b) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs for a person whose earnings are mainly commissions` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 10 21) EQUALS NOTHING   -- earnings are not mainly commissions
#ASSERT `reg 14(5)(b) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs for a person whose earnings are mainly commissions` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 10 21) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 14(5)(b) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs for a person whose earnings are mainly commissions` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 10 21) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 14(7) - less remunerative work (src:222)`

-- arguments: accepts less remunerative work with their employer; as a consequence receives a wage supplement under a provincial law; the last day of work before the less remunerative work begins
#ASSERT `reg 14(7) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs when less remunerative work is accepted` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 10 16) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 16)
#ASSERT `reg 14(7) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs when less remunerative work is accepted` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 10 16) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 14(7) the day on which an interruption of earnings occurs when less remunerative work is accepted` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 10 16) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no wage supplement

§ `Regulation 14 - the routes together (src:210-222)`

-- arguments: the answers under 14(1), 14(2), 14(5)(a), 14(5)(b), 14(7), 14(3), 14(4), 14(6)
#ASSERT `reg 14 an interruption of earnings has occurred` TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 14 an interruption of earnings has occurred` FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 10 18)) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 14 an interruption of earnings has occurred` FALSE NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 10 21)) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 14 an interruption of earnings has occurred` FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 10 21)) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 14 an interruption of earnings has occurred` FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 10 16)) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14 an interruption of earnings has occurred` FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)                      -- no route
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14 an interruption of earnings has occurred` TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE)                       -- a leave of 11(4)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14 an interruption of earnings has occurred` TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE)                       -- a pay period longer than a week
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14 an interruption of earnings has occurred` TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE)                       -- a leave of 11(3)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 14 an interruption of earnings has occurred` FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 10 18)) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE)    -- (3) is applied to the (2) route too (fork F12)

§ `Regulation 14.01 - the self-employed person (src:223)`

-- arguments: a self-employed person referred to in 152.07(1)(c); a day in the week of the declaration; normal level in hours per week; time given in the week; declares the reduction; ceases to work; the reason
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the day on which an interruption of earnings of a self-employed person occurs` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 21) 40 20 TRUE TRUE `er1 self-employed illness, injury or quarantine` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 18)
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the day on which an interruption of earnings of a self-employed person occurs` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 21) 40 23.9 TRUE TRUE `er1 self-employed pregnancy` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 18)         -- reduction 16.1 hours is more than 16
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the day on which an interruption of earnings of a self-employed person occurs` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 25) 40 0 TRUE TRUE `er1 self-employed need to provide care or support to a critically ill adult` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 25)
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the day on which an interruption of earnings of a self-employed person occurs` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 21) 40 24 TRUE TRUE `er1 self-employed illness, injury or quarantine` EQUALS NOTHING     -- exactly 40% (16 of 40 hours)
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the day on which an interruption of earnings of a self-employed person occurs` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 21) 40 20 FALSE TRUE `er1 self-employed illness, injury or quarantine` EQUALS NOTHING    -- no declaration
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the day on which an interruption of earnings of a self-employed person occurs` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 21) 40 20 TRUE FALSE `er1 self-employed illness, injury or quarantine` EQUALS NOTHING    -- did not cease to work
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the day on which an interruption of earnings of a self-employed person occurs` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 21) 40 20 TRUE TRUE `er1 self-employed another reason` EQUALS NOTHING                   -- a reason not listed
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the day on which an interruption of earnings of a self-employed person occurs` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 21) 0 0 TRUE TRUE `er1 self-employed illness, injury or quarantine` EQUALS NOTHING        -- no normal level to reduce
#ASSERT `reg 14.01 the day on which an interruption of earnings of a self-employed person occurs` FALSE (YMD 2026 10 21) 40 20 TRUE TRUE `er1 self-employed illness, injury or quarantine` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a self-employed person of 152.07(1)(c)
